  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion approach (the core hypothesis of this study) can outperform single-modality baselines, and which component choices yield a strong starting point. config_001 tests a well-motivated multimodal configuration: scvi_n200 (a well-established deep generative encoder for scRNA-seq), imagenet_vit_l (the stronger image encoder), avgpool (robust, low-variance aggregation), and weighted fusion (principled modality balancing). This establishes a strong baseline in the multimodal space. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual choices (RNA encoder, aggregation, fusion type) or compare against rna_only/image_only baselines. If it underperforms, we learn that multimodal fusion may not be the right direction and can pivot. As experiment 1 of 10, this maximizes information gain about the most fundamental design axis (modality combination) while using components most likely to perform well, avoiding a wasted experiment on a weak configuration."
}

